WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.577
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.378 --> 00:00:09.800
Many students, myself included,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.492
are worried about their test scores,
what advice do you have there?

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:19.078
This is probably the most frequently asked
question that I get is what about my GMAT

00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:20.613
score, what about my GRE?

00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:24.054
Well, we accept students with
a wide range of test scores and

00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:26.828
it is just one data point,
and I truly mean that.

00:00:26.828 --> 00:00:30.552
So, my best advice is,
well, we look at the tests.

00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:34.308
And they are important to ensure that
you're going to be able to thrive

00:00:34.308 --> 00:00:36.802
quantitatively and
verbally in the program.

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:40.801
So my best advice is, we look at it,
you should spend some time preparing.

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.792
What I hope for every applicant is,
when they submit that score, and

00:00:43.792 --> 00:00:44.883
I know it's stressful.

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:48.915
That you feel it's at least a decent
reflection of what your capabilities are,

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.150
so that's where the preparation comes in.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:55.932
That being said though, I know for many
students, test taking is not their forte.

00:00:55.932 --> 00:01:00.882
So, again, if there's a score honestly on
an application where it's far from maybe

00:01:00.882 --> 00:01:02.409
what our median might be.

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:06.129
And we do admit people in the 500s,
the 600s and the 700s, but

00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:09.551
if I see this may not be the strongest
point of their application.

00:01:09.551 --> 00:01:13.003
That's when I'm diving into the transcript
and seeing, again, how do they learn?

00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:14.670
Maybe tests just aren't their thing.

